% ============================================================================
% Specification-ambiguity VC instance  [EXERCISED 2026-07-28, check -k]
% ============================================================================
% Demonstrates the specification-ambiguity design-error class (vault C-048)
% via the enforced C7 (VCDM-conformance) error in spec_ambiguity.refinery.
%
% VC instance: IncomeCred is required to be VCDM-conformant (VcdmConformance
% annotation) but is assigned mdoc. mdoc (ISO 18013-5, CBOR/COSE) is treated
% as conformant under a permissive reading yet fails the VCDM 2.0
% JSON-LD/JSON data model -- the ambiguity the C7 error pins down.
%
% Expected result: UNSAT (vcdm_conformance_violation fires on IncomeCred).
% governance_conflict is deliberately NOT imported, isolating C7's error.
%
% Status (exercised 2026-07-28 with refinery-cli check -k, image digest
% sha256:88f1332e9aae356d91aef86aaaa3368be1b3931929fb3e10d87d65ab8a7fca8e):
%   -> "Inconsistencies found in model:
%     spec_ambiguity::vcdm_conformance_violation(IncomeCred, income_format):
%     error." Reproduced unchanged 2026-08-03 (vault A-008 / A-004).

import vc_metamodel.
import spec_ambiguity.
import csok_instance.

% Pin the open income format to mdoc (the non-VCDM-conformant reading).
MdocSchema(income_format).

% VCDM conformance required on IncomeCred.
VcdmConformance(vcdm_income).
VcdmConformance::target(vcdm_income, IncomeCred).

% Close governance (no other annotations generated).
!exists(EidasMandate::new).
!exists(PrivacyRequirement::new).
!exists(VcdmConformance::new).

% Base instance is 22 non-governance nodes (cf. csok_no_eidas: 28 = 22 + 6).
% One governance annotation added here. Widen if the solver reports 0 solutions.
scope node = 23, GovernanceAnnotation = 1.
